# Modern Design Guidelines

System rules for generating marketing assets: web pages, HTML emails, slides, documents, PDFs, social graphics. Layout architecture, spacing, type, color application, separation, motion.

**Brand palette, fonts, voice** → `luci-visual-design.mdc`, `luci-messaging-voice.mdc`, messaging guide. This doc governs **how** they are applied.

Rules are explicit and testable. Follow numbers and triggers literally. On conflict → **§9 Conflict resolution order**.

## Scope — do not apply retroactively

- **Use for new assets** and explicit redesign requests only.
- **Do not refactor** existing newsletter, emails, messaging docs, capability doc, review site, website prototypes, etc. unless the user asks.
- **Flagship reference:** `LUCI Systems Design System/ui_kits/newsletter/the-signal-issue-01-june-2026.html` — study rule *combination*, not pixels to copy. Fix known contrast issues per §4.2 when deriving new work.
- **Sales collateral (PDF-first docs):** follow `luci-sales-document-system.mdc` and start from `ui_kits/sales/_template-sales-document.html` + `sales-document.css` (prefix `doc-`). That rule canonizes the document spine, components, and prior design decisions so sales assets stay consistent.

---

## 0. How to use

**Step 1 — Pick track** by copy density, not file type:

> Count words a reader reads start-to-finish in the largest single section.
> - **> ~50 words sustained reading →** light canvas, near-black text. Track C dominates.
> - **≤ ~50 words, image-led/glanceable →** dark glassy OK. Track A or B.

Mixed assets: **zone canvas by section purpose** (dark masthead/index/callouts/closing; light reading sections — see §7).

**Step 2 — Apply in order:**
1. Foundation (§1–§5)
2. Track (§A / §B / §C)
3. Channel constraints (e.g. §C.5 email)

**Step 3 — Validate** against §8 checklist before output.

| Track | Use for | Canvas | Section |
|---|---|---|---|
| **A — Interactive** | Web, apps, hover/click/scroll | Dark OK | §A |
| **B — Static Visual** | Slides, social, heroes | Dark preferred | §B |
| **C — Static Document** | Reports, PDFs, long email | Light required | §C |

