## 1. Spacing system

- Base unit **8px**. Margins, padding, gaps: `8, 16, 24, 32, 40, 48, 64, 96, 128`.
- **4px** only legal half-step — tight type spacing (label-to-number, icon-to-text).
- **Never off-scale** (no 13px, 37px, 22px). Round to nearest 8 (or 4 for exception).
- Fluid: `clamp(min, vw, max)` where min/max are on-scale, e.g. `clamp(40px, 6vw, 64px)`.

## 2. Layout container

- **Reading measure hard constraint:** body copy **60–70 characters** → `max-width: 60ch` (or `650–680px`) on text blocks.
- Column may be wider (e.g. 820px) if running text inside stays ~60ch. **Decouple column width from text width** — separate variables.
- Side padding fluid: `clamp(28px, 6vw, 60px)`.

## 3. Typography

### 3.1 Three-tier font system (critical)

Three roles, three typefaces. Pick by **prominence**, not by element type.

**Tier 1 — Display (Syncopate). Short, high-impact only.**
- Masthead/wordmark, 1–3 word title, large numerals, small tracked uppercase labels (kickers, eyebrows, counters, role labels).
- **Hard limit: ≤3 words AND ≤~25 characters AND single line.**
- **Heuristic:** if text would wrap to line 2, or exceeds ~3 words → **not** display font. Use bold structure font.
- Never display font for article headlines, multi-line headers, sentences, sub-heads, running text.

**Tier 2 — Structure (Space Grotesk). Heads, labels, and metric numerals.**
- All real headlines, section titles, subheads, brand/proper names, prominent labels, kickers/eyebrows, and metric numerals (giant stats, totals, counts).
- Headlines/subheads: **700**, tracking `-0.025em` to `-0.015em`, line-height `1.1`.
- **Not** for running body copy — body copy is Inter (Tier 3).

**Tier 3 — Body + recede (Inter). All non-head copy, always.**
- **All running body copy / paragraph text / descriptions / decks / notes / attributions / table & list copy use Inter — in every asset** (documents, sales collateral, emails, web, hub). This is non-negotiable: copy text (non-head) is never Space Grotesk. Body: 400, line-height `1.5–1.72`.
- **Also the diagram/figure recede layer:** inside diagrams, illustrations, and figure-heavy art, set the small supporting text — data/node labels, captions, sub-labels, subtitles, axis/legend/annotation copy, vendor tags — in Inter so it recedes behind Space Grotesk names/titles.
- **Keep the prominent names/titles inside a diagram in Space Grotesk** (Tier 2); reserve Syncopate (Tier 1) for any true display word. A single diagram commonly uses all three tiers.
- All three families are embedded (subset, base64) in `assets/fonts/luci-brand-fonts.css` and directly in each canonical diagram SVG so they render offline, in PDF export, and when copied.

### 3.2 One display moment per asset
Exactly **one** display-scale element (typically masthead). Don't scatter multiple giant display headers.

### 3.3 Hierarchy through scale, not decoration
Size/weight contrast — not recoloring or font-switching mid-hierarchy. Tracked uppercase **kicker** above section titles.

### 3.4 Type scale (keep relationships; adapt sizes to brand fonts)

| Role | Font / weight | Size (web) | Size (doc/PDF) | LH | Tracking |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Display / masthead | Display 700 | clamp(52px,12vw,96px) | — | 0.9 | -0.03em |
| Oversized numeral | Display 700 | clamp(100px,22vw,200px) | — | 0.85 | — |
| Headline H1 | Head 700 | clamp(26px,4.5vw,38px) | 24–28pt | 1.1 | -0.025em |
| Marquee headline | Head 700 | clamp(30px,5vw,42px) | — | 1.1 | -0.025em |
| Subhead H2 | Head 700 | 20–24px | 16–18pt | 1.2 | -0.015em |
| Body | Body 400 | 17px (16–18) | 11–12pt | 1.5–1.72 | — |
| Pull quote | Body italic | clamp(19px,2.8vw,24px) | — | 1.45 | — |
| Kicker / label | Display 700 | 10–11px | 8–9pt | — | 0.20–0.22em UPPERCASE |
| Metric | Head 700 | 64px+ | — | 1.0–1.1 | label 11–12px under |
| Diagram label / caption (recede) | Recede 400–600 | 11–15px | — | 1.2–1.4 | 0 to 0.04em |

- "Display" = Tier 1 Syncopate · "Head" = Tier 2 Space Grotesk (headlines, labels, metric numerals) · "Body/Recede" = Tier 3 Inter (**all non-head copy** + diagram recede, per §3.1).
- Metric: giant number + small tracked uppercase label beneath.
- Heading line-heights (0.9–1.2) are **not** 8px-snapped. Body 1.5–1.72 is.

### 3.5 Section headers — the stacked lockup (site-wide standard)

Every titled section across the site **except the homepage** uses the `SectionBlock` **lockup variant**: `lockupName` (big, Space Grotesk 700, ~`clamp(34px,5vw,52px)`, left-aligned) → a 40px × 3px mint accent rule → `lockupRole` (small, 12px tracked uppercase; mint on dark, `--accent-light` on light). This is the diagram's own left-aligned stack order (name big, role small, name first), so a section that names a diagram component matches the image's emphasis exactly. Reveals on scroll — name rises, rule draws from the left, role settles in — with `prefers-reduced-motion` and `<noscript>` fallbacks.

Mapping existing two-string headers: the **shorter / label string → `lockupName`**, the **longer / descriptor string → `lockupRole`** (e.g. Platform §1: `lockupName="What LUCI is" lockupRole="Two forces working as one"`). For a section that only had a single `title`, keep it as `lockupName` and author a concise `lockupRole` subhead. No period on the name; the component uppercases the role, so enter it in normal case. **Avoid the inline `name | divider | role` arrangement** — it reads as an unbalanced single line next to short names.

## 4. Color application

Hex from brand palette. These are application rules (LUCI flagship tokens as examples).

### 4.1 Accent discipline
- Accent for **small elements only**: kickers, links, markers, one primary button, thin accent bars. **Never** body text or large accent fills.
- **Two accent values:**
  - **Bright** (e.g. mint `#68E3BE`) → **dark backgrounds only**
  - **Light-surface** (`#2b9e80`) → light backgrounds — the **canonized** light accent, used every time on white/off-white/light. (`#176B54` is retired; do not substitute it.)
- **Forbidden:** bright accent on light canvas (mint on sand = **1.23:1**).

### 4.2 Contrast (non-negotiable)

Targets: **AA 4.5:1** normal text; **3:1** large (≥24px or ≥18.66px bold).

| Pairing | Ratio | Verdict | Action |
|---|---|---|---|
| Body `#354F5C` on off-white/white/sand | 8.1 / 8.7 / 6.8 | ✅ | Keep |
| Off-white on navy | 15.1 | ✅ | Keep |
| Body-on-dark 88% white on navy | 11.6 | ✅ | Keep |
| Bright mint on navy / navy-deep | 10.2 / 11.6 | ✅ | Dark only |
| Light accent `#2b9e80` on off-white/white | ~3.1 | ✅ | Canonized light-surface accent (brand decision) |
| Light accent `#2b9e80` on sand | ~2.6 | ⚠️ | Canonized light accent; reads soft on sand — brand-accepted |
| Bright mint on sand/light | 1.23 | ❌ | **Forbidden** |

- **Small labels/links on light:** use **`#2b9e80`** — the canonized light-surface accent, every time. (`#176B54` is retired; do not substitute it.)
- Never color-only state — add text, icon, weight, or shape.

## 5. Separation & elevation

- Prefer **whitespace and background shifts** over lines. No heavy borders between blocks.
- **Soft shadows** when lifting: e.g. `0 24px 48px rgba(0,0,0,0.4)` on dark.
- **Radii:** cards/modules/images **12–24px**, consistent per asset. Pills/buttons **9999px**. Images match card radius.
- **Hairlines OK** on light: `~#D4D9DC` / 8% black; on dark `rgba(accent,0.15)`. Thin accent bars **2–4px** for major boundaries. De-boxed: hairline or tint, not container border.
- **Icons:** one library, uniform stroke; no mixed families per asset.

### 5.1 Soft-icon tiles + duotone icons (CANONICAL for icon-led points on light)

This is the **house style** for grouped points, cards, commitments, capability/architecture lists, and outcome rows on light canvases. Use it by default; do **not** revert to dark/heavy navy icon tiles or to a deep-green bar+label divider.

- **Tile:** ~**54px**, radius **16px**, soft gradient `linear-gradient(155deg,#E6F5EF 0%,#F3FAF8 100%)`, inset **1px** mint hairline `inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(43,158,128,0.14)`. No drop shadow, no dark fill.
- **Icon (duotone):** line icon, **primary strokes `#2b9e80`** (`--mint-dark`), with **one accent element in gold** `#CEB06E`/`--gold-deep`; optional 18–22% mint fill on the main shape. ~**28px**, stroke ~1.8. Each icon visually **distinct** (avoid four near-identical glyphs).
- **Copy:** Space Grotesk **bold** head (`--ink-strong`) + **Inter** body (`--navy-muted`). Optionally wrap each item in a **soft card**: same light gradient bg, 16px radius, inset mint hairline, ~26px padding.
- **Retire:** the deep-green **bar + uppercase-green label** section-divider treatment, and dark navy icon tiles on light pages. (`#176B54` is retired entirely; `#2b9e80` is the light accent but is never used as a bar+label section divider — use the §5.1 soft-icon tile pattern instead.)
- **Flow / phase connectors:** thick, **low-opacity gradient** (gold→mint), routed in the **margins** with **visible arrowheads** pointing inward to each row; never hidden behind nodes. Give the turn its **own vertical band** so it never competes with step labels.
- **Reference implementation:** `ui_kits/sales/capabilities-document.{html,css}` — `.doc-softicon`, case-study outcomes (p6), architecture points (p7), commitments + journey connector (p9).

